<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Asunción</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Asunción is the capital and largest city of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/paraguay">Paraguay</a>, on the east bank of the Paraguay river. Founded by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/juan-de-salazar">Juan de Salazar</a> in 1537, it was for decades the centre of Spanish settlement in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rio-de-la-plata">Río de la Plata</a> region, and from it <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/buenos-aires">Buenos Aires</a> was refounded in 1580. It became the capital of independent Paraguay in 1811.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/asuncion.jpg" alt="Asunción" width="320" height="256" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: MosheA · CC0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Palacio_de_los_L%C3%B3pez_Asunci%C3%B3n_2.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
